  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "One source for every HPE server",
      "items": [
        "OneView is the only HPE source whatever the iLO generation (4, 5 or 6): no BMC login, no per-generation branch (ADR-0022)",
        "What that costs on Gen10/Gen11 is written down, not worked around: cpu_threads only via /processors, GPU VRAM from the catalog",
        "One appliance, ~15 requests for the whole estate; the 2500-server ceiling is documented, not coded"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Settled on a live appliance, 2026-09-07",
      "items": [
        "821 servers, 685 profiles: nextPageUri paging fetched all 685, so the 256 cap is per request, no sharding",
        "Omitting X-Api-Version silently serves an older schema (server-hardware-1 vs -12, both 200) \u2014 the header is always sent",
        "iLO 5/6 populate memoryMb/processorCount near-universally (797/797, 24/24); 140 members with no profile are skipped by design"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Still open",
      "items": [
        "GPU mapping is unverified: no GPU-bearing HPE host exists in the estate, so no Devices entry has ever reported DeviceType GPU",
        "Whether AMS was running was not established; the profile name stays the only field trusted for ProviderServer.name",
        "count=-1 means 64 on /rest/server-profiles \u2014 an explicit count is always sent and truncation is reported as a PARTIAL run"
      ]
    }
  ]
